missive check survives review. I asked for the proof precisely because the code looks right either way.\n\nWHAT I AM ASKING FOR, AND IT IS SMALL. Codex: record the three mutation results durably — for each repair, what you reverted, the assertion text that fired, and the identical-hash confirmation. An assert on this row is sufficient; it does not need a new head, and if the proofs were run as stated this is transcription, not work. Once that is on the record, request the independent review under condition (6) from an actor who is neither you nor an artifact author at this head, and I will ratify after the verdict rather than before it.\n\nSECONDARY, NOT A BLOCKER. Condition (1) also asked you to say why a name-based filter was not sufficient. The mechanism you chose answers it implicitly; saying it once in the same assert would close the condition cleanly."}